      "label": "Helping Guest in Crisis",
      "quote": "I helped her take her luggage up to the room, and saw her rummaging in her bag for formula, so I went down to the convenience store, bought a carton of milk, warmed it up in hot water and took it up to her."
    },
    {
      "label": "Staff Recognition and Pride",
      "quote": "HR made a copy and put it up on the noticeboard in the staff corridor. When I walked past after my shift, I stood there and looked at it for a while and took a photo."
    },
    {
      "label": "Humility and Downplaying Achievements",
      "quote": "But honestly, anyone would have done the same in that situation. There’s nothing special about it. You don’t need to put it in specially."
    },
    {
      "label": "Emotional Impact of Positive Feedback",
      "quote": "I didn’t get to sleep until very late that night, and the next day I got to the hotel forty minutes early. I changed and stood in the lobby, and when the manager came in he asked whether I’d got my shift wrong."
    },
    {
      "label": "Ongoing Monitoring of Recognition",
      "quote": "Now whenever I push the luggage trolley past the noticeboard, I take a look to see if it’s still there. Last week they put up a new batch on the noticeboard and mine got moved into the corner, so I moved it back towards the middle."
    }
  ],
  "interpretation": "The interviewee reflects on a positive guest interaction where he helped a stressed parent, which led to recognition. He feels pride in his actions but downplays his efforts, showing humility and a desire to maintain his professional demeanor.",
  "tone": "positive",
  "confidence": 95
}

